<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Comerci cut.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Comerci cut.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- Dresdner Kleinwort Benson said on Tuesday analyst Justin McGowan had cut his rating for Controladora Comercial Mexicana SA, or Comerci, to sell from hold.</p>
<p>-- In a report, McGowan said he was downgrading the stock because of Comerci's plan to buy the Mexican operations of Kmart Corp for $148.5 million and the breakup of Comerci's joint venture with France's Groupe Auchan.</p>
<p>-- He cut his 1997 forecast for earnings per share to 0.65 peso from 0.72. Estimates for 1998 earnings per share remain at 0.74 peso.</p>
<p>-- The company's shares were off 0.50 peso to 6.40 in Mexico City.</p>
<p>((--Ian Simpson, Wall Street desk, (212) 859-1879))</p>
